7"},{"key":"ref16","first-page":"1","article-title":"Modeling and control of aggregated heterogeneous thermostatically controlled loads for ancillary services","volume-title":"Proc. PSCC","author":"Koch","year":"2011"},{"key":"ref17","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1109\/LCSYS.2022.3188535"},{"key":"ref18","first-page":"1:16","article-title":"Verification of neural reachable tubes via scenario optimization and conformal prediction","volume-title":"Proceedings of Machine Learning Research","author":"Lin","year":"2024"},{"key":"ref19","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1109\/LRA.2023.3292071"},{"key":"ref20","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1145\/3576841.3585927"},{"key":"ref21","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1109\/tac.2023.3346793"},{"key":"ref22","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1109\/CDC49753.2023.10383723"},{"key":"ref23","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1007\/3-540-36755-1_29"},{"key":"ref24","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1109\/LCSYS.2022.3186187"},{"key":"ref25","author":"Qin","year":"2023","journal-title":"Conformance testing for stochastic cyber-physical systems"},{"key":"ref26","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1109\/ICCPS54341.2022.00017"},{"key":"ref27","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1016\/j.sysconle.2014.08.005"},{"key":"ref28","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1109\/CDC.2015.7403294"},{"issue":"3","key":"ref29","article-title":"A tutorial on conformal prediction","volume":"9","author":"Shafer","year":"2008","journal-title":"Journal of Machine Learning Research"},{"key":"ref30","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1007\/978-1-4419-0224-5"},{"key":"ref31","first-page":"194","article-title":"Data-driven reachability using christoffel functions and conformal prediction","volume-title":"Conformal and Probabilistic Prediction with Applications","author":"Tebjou","year":"2023"},{"key":"ref32","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1007\/s10994-013-5355-6"},{"key":"ref33","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1007\/b106715"}],"event":{"name":"2024 European Control Conference (ECC)","location":"Stockholm, Sweden","start":{"date-parts":[[2024,6,25]]},"end":{"date-parts":[[2024,6,28]]}},"container-title":["2024 European Control Conference (ECC)"],"link":[{"URL":"http:\/\/xplorestaging.ieee.org\/ielx8\/10590709\/10590710\/10590827.pdf?arnumber=10590827","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"similarity-checking"}],"deposited":{"date-parts":[[2024,7,25]],"date-time":"2024-07-25T06:01:54Z","timestamp":1721887314000},"score":31.875444,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/ieeexplore.ieee.org\/document\/10590827\/"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2024,6,25]]},"references-count":33,"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.23919\/ecc64448.2024.10590827","published":{"date-parts":[[2024,6,25]]}},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,6]],"date-time":"2026-10-06T15:53:22Z","timestamp":1791302002275,"version":"4.1.0"},"publisher-location":"Cham","reference-count":19,"publisher":"Springer Nature Switzerland","isbn-type":[{"value":"9783032411594","type":"print"},{"value":"9783032411600","type":"electronic"}],"license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,7]],"date-time":"2026-10-07T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1791331200000},"content-version":"tdm","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"https:\/\/creativecommons.org\/licenses\/by\/4.0"},{"start":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,7]],"date-time":"2026-10-07T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1791331200000},"content-version":"vor","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"https:\/\/creativecommons.org\/licenses\/by\/4.0"}],"content-domain":{"domain":["link.springer.com"],"crossmark-restriction":false},"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2027]]},"abstract":"<jats:title>Abstract<\/jats:title>\n                  <jats:p>Constructing correct Signal Temporal Logic (STL) specifications from informal requirements is a challenging task, due to the ambiguous and imprecise nature of natural language descriptions. Witness traces can support requirements elicitation and validation by providing concrete behavioral examples that satisfy or violate a specification. However, naive generation of traces from a specification can result in behaviors that are not plausible.<\/jats:p>\n                  <jats:p>We present a method for generating semantically meaningful witnesses for STL specifications by explicitly incorporating domain knowledge into the generation process. The approach uses signal templates representing common CPS behaviors to constrain the space of generated traces and formulates witness generation as an optimization problem. The resulting framework supports the generation of both satisfying and violating witnesses, as well as differential witnesses that expose behavioral differences between alternative STL specifications. We further combine witness generation with explainable trace diagnostics to facilitate requirements elicitation, specification validation, and the comparison of alternative specifications. We illustrate the approach on representative CPS examples.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1007\/978-3-032-41160-0_25","type":"book-chapter","created":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,6]],"date-time":"2026-10-06T15:01:30Z","timestamp":1791298890000},"page":"404-421","update-policy":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1007\/springer_crossmark_policy","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["STL-Witness: Signal Generation from\u00a0STL Specifications"],"prefix":"10.1007","author":[{"given":"Dejan","family":"Ni\u010dkovi\u0107","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"member":"297","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,7]]},"reference":[{"key":"25_CR1","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","unstructured":"Bartocci, E., Ferr\u00e8re, T., Manjunath, N., Ni\u010dkovi\u0107, D.: Localizing faults in simulink\/stateflow models with STL. In: Prandini, M., Deshmukh, J.V. (eds.) Proceedings of the 21st International Conference on Hybrid Systems: Computation and Control (part of CPS Week), HSCC 2018,